WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.660
Color is a powerful cue that convolutional networks
readily exploit for object recognition,

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:11.401
but it becomes a liability when the colors seen at
test time differ from those in training.

00:00:11.481 --> 00:00:15.501
This paper introduces Color Equivariant
Convolutions, or CEConvs,

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:21.178
a new building block that shares shape features
across the color spectrum while preserving

00:00:21.258 --> 00:00:23.260
discriminative color information.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.919
By hard-wiring parameter sharing over discrete hue shifts,

00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:33.984
CEConvs let networks like ResNets generalize to
underrepresented colors and stay robust to test-time hue shifts,

00:00:34.064 --> 00:00:35.750
without throwing color away.
